  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have an array A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​] of size NNN.\n\nPerform **exactly** KKK operations of the type:\n\nPick index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N) and,\n\n\nIf AiA_iAi​ is even, replace AiA_iAi​ by Ai2\\frac{A_i}{2}2Ai​​\nIf AiA_iAi​ is odd, replace AiA_iAi​ by Ai+1A_i+1Ai​+1\nFind the maximum possible sum of the array AAA after all KKK operations are complete. Note that you aren't allowed to skip operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of 222 lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 integers NNN and KKK, the size of the array AAA and the number of operations.\nThe next line contains NNN integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible final sum of the array AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤5⋅105",
      "2≤N≤1062 \\leq N \\leq 10^62≤N≤106",
      "1≤Ai,K&lt;2431 \\le A_i, K \\lt 2^{43}1≤Ai​,K&lt;243",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "It can be shown that the answer doesn't exceed the limit of a signed 646464-bit integer"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
